PDFKit
------

The document writer is a Lua port of PDFKit 0.20.2 by Devon Govett
(https://github.com/foliojs/pdfkit, https://pdfkit.org/). PDFKit is
Copyright (c) 2014 Devon Govett and is licensed under the MIT license.
A copy of that license is in vendor/pdfkit/LICENSE. The conditions that
matter here: the copyright notice and this permission notice shall be
included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

The notices below name the libraries the Lua was transcribed from, and the
assets this tree ships. vendor/pdfkit/ is the upstream reading copy and the
Node oracle. It is not part of the Lua rock.

Transcribed libraries
---------------------

Filled in by the license audit.

zlib
----

src/lua-pdfkit/zlib/deflate.lua, src/lua-pdfkit/zlib/trees.lua, and
src/lua-pdfkit/flate.lua are a transcription of zlib 1.3.1. The zlib
license notice is recorded here once the audit quotes it.

Standard fonts
--------------

The fourteen standard-font metric modules are numbers derived from the
Adobe AFM files PDFKit 0.20.2 generates from. The raw .afm files are not
installed by the rock. Adobe's copyright notice is recorded here once the
audit quotes it.

ICC profile
-----------

PDF/A output embeds the sRGB IEC61966-2.1 profile when a document needs it.
The HP/Microsoft notice is recorded here if 0.20.2 still ships that profile.

Test fonts and images
---------------------

Fonts and images under test/assets/ are used by the comparator. They are
not installed by the rock. Each one is named here, or in
test/assets/NOTICE, once the audit finishes.
